## 1. Context

CW-002E proves that unrestricted rational weighted pair synchronization is undecidable.

This immediately raises the structural question:

> Which old regularity assumptions destroy the undecidability mechanism?

Rabin's 1963 paper already isolated a special class of probabilistic automata in which all transition probabilities are strictly positive. He called these "actual automata" and proved strong stability/definiteness properties.

For synchronization, strict positivity gives an even simpler exact boundary.

