# 4. Explicit finite reset bound

For

\[
0<\varepsilon<TV(p,q),
\]

any word of length

\[
\boxed{
k
\ge
\frac{
\log(\varepsilon/TV(p,q))
}{
\log\rho
}
}
\]

satisfies

\[
TV(pP_w,qP_w)\le\varepsilon.
\]

Thus the universal sufficient integer horizon is

\[
\boxed{
L_\varepsilon
\le
\left\lceil
\frac{
\log(\varepsilon/TV(p,q))
}{
\log(1-n\eta)
}
\right\rceil.
}
\]

If \(p=q\), the threshold is zero.

This is the exact opposite of CW-002E's anti-Černý result.

Under unrestricted rational stochastic generators there is no recursive witness-length bound.

Under strict positivity there is an explicit logarithmic bound and every word of that length succeeds.

