# 5. Positivity is stronger than necessary

The proof uses only a uniform Dobrushin contraction bound.

Therefore strict positivity can be replaced by

\[
\boxed{
\bar\delta
:=
\max_a\delta(P_a)
<1.
}
\]

Then

\[
TV(pP_w,qP_w)
\le
\bar\delta^{|w|}
TV(p,q).
\]

So the true structural sufficient condition is:

\[
\boxed{
\text{every generator is uniformly scrambling.}
}
\]

Strict positivity is a simple Rabin-style sufficient condition.

This produces a hierarchy:

\[
\text{strictly positive}
\subset
\text{uniformly scrambling}
\subset
\text{general stochastic}.
\]

The first two admit immediate pair-synchronization bounds.

The general class is undecidable.

