# 7. Algorithmic phase diagram

We can now state a sharper boundary.

## Deterministic exact synchronization

Finite-state/combinatorial; existence decidable. Reset-threshold optimization is hard, with the Černý conjecture governing worst-case length.

## General stochastic global synchronization

\[
v_{\rm glob}=0
\]

is decidable through scrambling/support semigroups.

## Uniformly scrambling stochastic pair synchronization

Always converges exponentially; explicit finite horizon.

## General rational stochastic pair synchronization

Even fixed-threshold reachability such as

\[
TV<1/2
\]

is undecidable.

Thus adding stochastic weights does not monotonically increase difficulty.

The decisive issue is whether a finite support/contraction certificate survives.

